{"duration_api_ms":116318,"stop_reason":"tool_use","session_id":"0cb31384-061d-4a77-8066-d07b22459577","total_cost_usd":0.6192126,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":105369,"cache_read_input_tokens":105773,"output_tokens":10534,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":5512},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":105369,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2452,"cache_read_input_tokens":101451,"cache_creation_input_tokens":8240,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":8240},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":71149,"outputTokens":17,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.071234,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000,"thinkingTokens":0,"canonicalModel":"claude-haiku-4-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"},"claude-sonnet-5":{"inputTokens":4,"outputTokens":10534,"cacheReadInputTokens":105773,"cacheCreationInputTokens":105369,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.5479786,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"thinkingTokens":5512,"canonicalModel":"claude-sonnet-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":3,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"requirements\":[{\"id\":\"transit-networks\",\"requirement\":\"Two independent transit networks exist between node1 and node2\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"node1 eth1/eth2 configured with 10.10.1.1/30 and 10.10.2.1/30; node2 vtnet1/vtnet2 configured with 10.10.1.2/30 and 10.10.2.2/30 (persisted into OPNsense config.xml as opt1/opt2 with pf pass rules). Both links independently ping successfully, and post-restart re-verification confirms both remain up and addressed correctly.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-8331ba2d1d8b4837\",\"cmd-0e1246c1d2f24128\",\"cmd-8268a95cb1a24562\",\"cmd-aff92f28bd05455d\",\"cmd-613647f54c904957\",\"cmd-7a8e5ce53ea5457f\"]},{\"id\":\"port-8080-transit1\",\"requirement\":\"TCP port 8080 traffic from node3 to node4 is steered exclusively across transit network 1\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"VyOS PBR on node1 (fwmark 0x7fffff9a -> table 101 -> eth1/transit1) combined with node3-side marking/routing to next-hop node1. Final clean tcpdump capture on node1 shows the full 8080 handshake plus payload appearing only on eth1 (transit1) and not on eth2 (transit2); confirmed again after the full restart cycle.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-7f042d6ecf6e4b5b\",\"cmd-0146efade35c4627\",\"cmd-fdc40fb4b0f94e75\"]},{\"id\":\"port-9090-transit2\",\"requirement\":\"TCP port 9090 traffic from node3 to node4 is steered exclusively across transit network 2\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"PBR fwmark 0x7fffff99 -> table 102 -> eth2/transit2. Final clean tcpdump capture shows the full 9090 handshake plus payload only on eth2, not eth1; confirmed again post-restart.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-7f042d6ecf6e4b5b\",\"cmd-0146efade35c4627\",\"cmd-fdc40fb4b0f94e75\"]},{\"id\":\"reach-node4\",\"requirement\":\"Both flows actually reach node4 (end-to-end delivery, not just to node1/node2)\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"node4-side listener logs (rx8080.log / rx9090.log) contain the application payload for both ports, both in the initial test and after all four nodes were restarted (rx logs show recovered deliveries such as 'node1-recovered-8080/9090' and 'ALL-RESTARTED-8080/9090').\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-0146efade35c4627\",\"cmd-0f759009e452499e\"]},{\"id\":\"demonstrate-path\",\"requirement\":\"Demonstrate which transit network carried each flow\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"Simultaneous per-interface tcpdump captures on node1 (eth1 filtered to port 8080, eth2 filtered to port 9090, and earlier unfiltered captures on both) directly show port-based segregation across the two transit links, satisfying the 'show which network carried each flow' requirement.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-7f042d6ecf6e4b5b\",\"cmd-fdc40fb4b0f94e75\"]}],\"confidence\":0.9,\"operational_hygiene\":{\"score\":0.7,\"summary\":\"Most state-changing commands were clearly tied to building the transit networks, PBR/marking configuration, or bounded evidence collection, and packet-capture files were cleaned up on node1/node2 (cmd-2017511b8a3b464d, cmd-4a756da2e4744f6e, cmd-04f8a5e9ea834781). However, several artifacts were left behind on node4 with no final cleanup: nc8080.pid, nc9090.pid, node4.pcap, td4.log/pid, reboot.log, and socat8080.log/socat9090.log persist in the after-executor snapshot (rx8080.log/rx9090.log are still in active use by the persistent echo8080/echo9090 services, so their retention is expected, but the pid/pcap/log files are stale residue with no cleanup command executed). Separately, the mandatory restart protocol left NetworkManager-wait-online.service in a failed state on both node3 and node4 post-reboot (systemctl is-system-running reported 'degraded' on node3, cmd-07b19b08bd924b42), and while the executor correctly diagnosed and fixed the resulting functional impact (pbr-egress.service and echo8080/echo9090 not autostarting), it did not remediate or mask the underlying failed unit, leaving the node in a degraded systemd state. The pfctl state-kill on node2 (cmd-e575258e0f424197) was a bounded, low-risk troubleshooting mutation.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-04f8a5e9ea834781\",\"cmd-2017511b8a3b464d\",\"cmd-4a756da2e4744f6e\",\"cmd-07b19b08bd924b42\",\"cmd-e575258e0f424197\",\"global:after_executor:node4:temporary-files\",\"global:after_executor:node3:failed-services\",\"global:after_executor:node4:failed-services\"]},\"overall_summary\":\"The executor built two independent VyOS/OPNsense transit networks and used VyOS policy-based routing (fwmark + separate routing tables) combined with node3-side marking to steer node3->node4 TCP/8080 exclusively over transit1 and TCP/9090 exclusively over transit2, with per-interface tcpdump captures on node1 directly demonstrating the segregation and node4-side listener logs confirming end-to-end delivery of both flows. All material outcomes are satisfied with direct, non-conflicting evidence, and the mandatory node-restart protocol was executed on all four nodes with genuine pre/post boot-identity changes, an observed real disruption (PBR/listener services failing to autostart due to a NetworkManager-wait-online dependency), a diagnosed fix, and confirmed post-restart recovery of both traffic-steering behavior and end-to-end delivery.\",\"limitations\":[\"NetworkManager-wait-online.service remained in a failed state on node3 and node4 after restart, leaving systemd reporting 'degraded' on at least node3; the executor fixed the functional symptoms but did not resolve or explicitly acknowledge this underlying degraded state.\",\"Several temporary test/verification artifacts (pid files, a pcap, and reboot/tcpdump logs) were left on node4 without a final cleanup command, unlike node1 and node2 where cleanup was explicitly performed.\",\"The after_prepare snapshot is an alias of before_prepare (prepare was disabled), so no separate preparer-vs-executor baseline distinction was possible beyond the fixed before/after-executor comparison already used.\"]}","structured_output":{"requirements":[{"id":"transit-networks","requirement":"Two independent transit networks exist between node1 and node2","status":"satisfied","summary":"node1 eth1/eth2 c