h transit network carried each flow","status":"satisfied","summary":"Simultaneous per-interface tcpdump captures on node1 (eth1 filtered to port 8080, eth2 filtered to port 9090, and earlier unfiltered captures on both) directly show port-based segregation across the two transit links, satisfying the 'show which network carried each flow' requirement.","evidence_ids":["cmd-7f042d6ecf6e4b5b","cmd-fdc40fb4b0f94e75"]}],"confidence":0.9,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.7,"summary":"Most state-changing commands were clearly tied to building the transit networks, PBR/marking configuration, or bounded evidence collection, and packet-capture files were cleaned up on node1/node2 (cmd-2017511b8a3b464d, cmd-4a756da2e4744f6e, cmd-04f8a5e9ea834781). However, several artifacts were left behind on node4 with no final cleanup: nc8080.pid, nc9090.pid, node4.pcap, td4.log/pid, reboot.log, and socat8080.log/socat9090.log persist in the after-executor snapshot (rx8080.log/rx9090.log are still in active use by the persistent echo8080/echo9090 services, so their retention is expected, but the pid/pcap/log files are stale residue with no cleanup command executed). Separately, the mandatory restart protocol left NetworkManager-wait-online.service in a failed state on both node3 and node4 post-reboot (systemctl is-system-running reported 'degraded' on node3, cmd-07b19b08bd924b42), and while the executor correctly diagnosed and fixed the resulting functional impact (pbr-egress.service and echo8080/echo9090 not autostarting), it did not remediate or mask the underlying failed unit, leaving the node in a degraded systemd state. The pfctl state-kill on node2 (cmd-e575258e0f424197) was a bounded, low-risk troubleshooting mutation.","evidence_ids":["cmd-04f8a5e9ea834781","cmd-2017511b8a3b464d","cmd-4a756da2e4744f6e","cmd-07b19b08bd924b42","cmd-e575258e0f424197","global:after_executor:node4:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node3:failed-services","global:after_executor:node4:failed-services"]},"overall_summary":"The executor built two independent VyOS/OPNsense transit networks and used VyOS policy-based routing (fwmark + separate routing tables) combined with node3-side marking to steer node3->node4 TCP/8080 exclusively over transit1 and TCP/9090 exclusively over transit2, with per-interface tcpdump captures on node1 directly demonstrating the segregation and node4-side listener logs confirming end-to-end delivery of both flows. All material outcomes are satisfied with direct, non-conflicting evidence, and the mandatory node-restart protocol was executed on all four nodes with genuine pre/post boot-identity changes, an observed real disruption (PBR/listener services failing to autostart due to a NetworkManager-wait-online dependency), a diagnosed fix, and confirmed post-restart recovery of both traffic-steering behavior and end-to-end delivery.","limitations":["NetworkManager-wait-online.service remained in a failed state on node3 and node4 after restart, leaving systemd reporting 'degraded' on at least node3; the executor fixed the functional symptoms but did not resolve or explicitly acknowledge this underlying degraded state.","Several temporary test/verification artifacts (pid files, a pcap, and reboot/tcpdump logs) were left on node4 without a final cleanup command, unlike node1 and node2 where cleanup was explicitly performed.","The after_prepare snapshot is an alias of before_prepare (prepare was disabled), so no separate preparer-vs-executor baseline distinction was possible beyond the fixed before/after-executor comparison already used."]},"ttft_ms":74514,"type":"result","duration_ms":114476,"uuid":"b7ccd6eb-259c-4bca-8d79-593818e15d40","ttft_stream_ms":2537,"time_to_request_ms":38,"first_content_frame_ms":2781,"queued_turn_count":0}
